{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Optional capability a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PlayerAdapter","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" implements when its player owns"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"picture-in-picture natively."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PictureInPictureCapable"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/optiviewadscore\/pictureinpicturecapable"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PictureInPictureCapable\/isPictureInPicture()","doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PictureInPictureCapable\/onPictureInPictureChange(_:)","doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PictureInPictureCapable\/setPictureInPicture(_:)"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Player-contract","identifiers":["doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PlayerAdapter","doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PlayerAdapterEvent","doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/TimedMetadataCue","doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/ContentVideoSizeProvider"],"title":"Player contract","generated":true}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore"]]},"metadata":{"title":"PictureInPictureCapable","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PictureInPictureCapable"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PictureInPictureCapable"}],"externalID":"s:15OptiViewAdsCore09PictureInE7CapableP","modules":[{"name":"OptiViewAdsCore"}],"symbolKind":"protocol","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Protocol"},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PictureInPictureCapable"},{"kind":"text","text":" : AnyObject"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The runtime’s default is to drive "},{"code":"AVPictureInPictureController","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" against the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"content "},{"code":"AVPlayerLayer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" it discovers in the integrator’s view hierarchy."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"That works for players that keep one layer alive across source changes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(AVPlayer: the SDK swaps the ITEM on the same player), and breaks for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"players that rebuild their internal pipeline on a source change: THEOplayer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"replaces its internal AVPlayer\/layer when "},{"code":"source","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is assigned, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"discovered layer dies, and AVKit closes the window at the exact moment the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SDK lends the content player to the ad. Measured on the iOS e2e fleet"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(catalog-pip, SDK 0.50.0-beta.500): the window opened before the break and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closed at "},{"code":"adbreakbegin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with the ad playing full-screen in the main"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"window instead of inside it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Such players expose their own picture-in-picture facility with the missing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"piece — THEOplayer retains the window across source changes when the host"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constructs it with "},{"code":"PiPConfiguration(retainPresentationModeOnSourceChange: true)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — but only if the window is driven through THAT facility. This"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"protocol is how an adapter hands the SDK that steering wheel; the renderer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"prefers it over its own controller whenever the content adapter conforms."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All three members are called on the main thread (the renderer is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"); the change handler must likewise be invoked on the main"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thread, for every transition — including viewer-driven ones (the system UI"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can dismiss the window at any time), which is the whole reason the handler"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exists: the break format follows what is actually on screen."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore/documentation/OptiViewAdsCore/PictureInPictureCapable/isPictureInPicture()":{"title":"isPictureInPicture()","identifier":"doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PictureInPictureCapable\/isPictureInPicture()","url":"\/documentation\/optiviewadscore\/pictureinpicturecapable\/ispictureinpicture()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether the player is presenting in picture-in-picture right now —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read from the player, not from the last request."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isPictureInPicture"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","required":true},"doc://optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore/documentation/OptiViewAdsCore/ContentVideoSizeProvider":{"url":"\/documentation\/optiviewadscore\/contentvideosizeprovider","kind":"symbol","title":"ContentVideoSizeProvider","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Optional capability for reporting the content video’s intrinsic dimensions."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ContentVideoSizeProvider"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/ContentVideoSizeProvider","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ContentVideoSizeProvider"}]},"doc://optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore/documentation/OptiViewAdsCore/PlayerAdapterEvent":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PlayerAdapterEvent","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Event types a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PlayerAdapter"},{"type":"text","text":" forwards (mirrors the Kotlin "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PlayerAdapterEvent"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"title":"PlayerAdapterEvent","url":"\/documentation\/optiviewadscore\/playeradapterevent","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PlayerAdapterEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PlayerAdapterEvent"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore/documentation/OptiViewAdsCore/TimedMetadataCue":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A single in